(SURYAPATH RAILWAYS \(SPR\) — FICTIONAL PASSENGER CANCELLATION AND REFUND POLICY) Tj T*
(POLICY V1 | EFFECTIVE 2026-01-01 00:00 IST | END: 2026-04-30) Tj T*
(This is a fictional policy, not an Indian Railways rule. Currency: Indian rupees \(INR\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(P-01. VERSION AND CONTRACT DATE) Tj T*
(The booking date \(the calendar date of successful ticket purchase in IST\) fixes the governing) Tj T*
(policy version for the entire booking. A cancellation or departure after a new version starts) Tj T*
(does not migrate an older booking. This policy governs bookings made from 2026-01-01 through) Tj T*
(2026-04-30. All dates and clocks in this document use IST. A booking made at 00:00 IST on an) Tj T*
(effective date belongs to the new version, not the prior one. A booking cannot be retroactively) Tj T*
(switched to a later version.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(P-02. DEFINITIONS AND PRIORITY) Tj T*
("Base fare" means the per-passenger ticket fare, excluding the non-refundable booking service) Tj T*
(fee and any independent food purchases. "T" is the exact time between receipt of a valid) Tj T*
(voluntary cancellation request and the TRAIN'S SCHEDULED departure from that passenger's origin) Tj T*
(station; it is measured in hours and minutes, not rounded. 'At least' includes the threshold) Tj T*
(exactly. "Confirmed" and "waitlisted" refer to passenger-level status when a voluntary) Tj T*
(cancellation is requested; for automatic waitlist processing, use final status at departure.) Tj T*
("Premium QuickBook" \(PQ\) is a special quota, not a separate travel class. Exception clauses) Tj T*
(E1–E4 override the ordinary provisions where their exact conditions are met; the claimant cannot) Tj T*
(combine deductions or collect two refunds for the same ticket.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(P-03. ORDINARY VOLUNTARY CANCELLATION: CONFIRMED NON-PREMIUM TICKETS) Tj T*
(Use the passenger's base fare and class. The table gives the cancellation CHARGE, not the) Tj T*
(refund. Refund = max\(0, base fare minus charge\). For any flat charge, deduct no more than the) Tj T*
(passenger's base fare. No refund of base fare is due when T is below the last threshold,) Tj T*
(including after departure. The booking service fee is not refunded under this clause.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CLASS                T >= 48 h         12 <= T < 48 h        4 <= T < 12 h       T <  4 h) Tj T*
(AC First \(1A\)        INR 240          INR 120              50% of base fare     No refund) Tj T*
(AC Two Tier \(2A\)     INR 200          INR 100              50% of base fare     No refund) Tj T*
(Sleeper \(SL\)         INR 120          INR 60               50% of base fare     No refund) Tj T*
(Second Sitting \(2S\)  INR 60           INR 30               50% of base fare     No refund) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(P-04. BOOKING SERVICE FEE AND OTHER CHARGES) Tj T*
(SPR collects INR 20 per booking reference \(PNR\), once per original booking and not once per) Tj T*
(passenger. It is separate from every base fare. No additional "processing", "gateway",) Tj T*
("reinstatement", or "expedited refund" charge is imposed by SPR. The original booking service) Tj T*
(fee is never returned on a normal voluntary, waitlist, premium, or medical cancellation; only) Tj T*
(exceptions expressly saying otherwise can refund it. Multiple cancelled passengers do not) Tj T*
(multiply the booking service fee.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(P-05. PREMIUM QUICKBOOK \(PQ\) TICKETS) Tj T*
(No voluntary refund is available for a confirmed Premium QuickBook ticket at any time before or) Tj T*
(after departure. This special rule replaces P-03 for a confirmed PQ passenger regardless of 1A,) Tj T*
(2A, SL, or 2S class. An unconfirmed PQ waitlisted passenger instead follows P-06. A booking) Tj T*
(becomes PQ only if sold explicitly under the PQ quota; paying a high fare alone does not make it) Tj T*
(PQ. E1 and E2 can override the confirmed-PQ rule, and E3 can override it only where that version) Tj T*
(expressly permits.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(P-06. WAITLISTED TICKETS) Tj T*
(A still-waitlisted passenger may voluntarily cancel while T >= 4 hours and receives the full) Tj T*
(base fare less a flat clerkage of INR 20 \(but not below zero\), irrespective of class and PQ) Tj T*
(quota; the service fee stays non-refundable. For T < 4 hours voluntary cancellation is closed) Tj T*
(for waitlisted passengers. However, a passenger still waitlisted at scheduled departure is) Tj T*
(automatically refunded base fare less that same INR 20 clerkage, without any request, even if) Tj T*
(the passenger missed the voluntary cancellation cutoff. A passenger promoted to confirmed status) Tj T*
(before requesting cancellation must use P-03 or P-05 instead; if confirmed by departure, no) Tj T*
(automatic waitlist refund is due. SPR has no guarantee of promotion from waitlist to confirmed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(P-07. PARTIAL CANCELLATIONS AND SEPARATE PASSENGER STATUS) Tj T*
(Voluntary partial cancellation is supported only when the original PNR has at least 3 passengers) Tj T*
(and at least 2 passenger\(s\) remain active after the request. Each cancelled passenger is) Tj T*
(assessed independently by class, PQ quota, base fare, and current confirmation status; never) Tj T*
(apply a single percentage or one clerkage to the combined PNR fare. The booking fee of INR 20) Tj T*
(remains a single non-refundable fee on the PNR. A request that cancels every passenger is a full) Tj T*
(cancellation, not an eligible partial cancellation, and is evaluated passenger by passenger) Tj T*
ET
