(under the applicable provisions. Once a passenger is removed from the PNR, that cancellation) Tj T*
(cannot be reversed; a fresh ticket is needed to travel.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(P-08. CLAIM SUBMISSION, PROOF AND PROCESSING) Tj T*
(A voluntary request must reach SPR's online cancellation channel before scheduled departure and) Tj T*
(within the respective eligibility window. E1–E4 use their own deadlines. Claimants must identify) Tj T*
(the booking reference, the affected passenger, and the reason for invoking an exception.) Tj T*
(Accepted refunds return to the original payment source; SPR does not promise instant credit, a) Tj T*
(particular number of banking days, cash payout on demand, or preferential refund processing.) Tj T*
(Claims are subject to verification; a request alone is not a promise of approval. Food and) Tj T*
(third-party purchases are outside the scope of this policy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(E1. OPERATOR-CANCELLED SERVICE — OVERRIDES P-03, P-05, P-06, P-07 DEADLINES) Tj T*
(If SPR cancels the passenger's scheduled train, an affected passenger who files a claim no later) Tj T*
(than 7 calendar days after scheduled departure receives 100% of that passenger's base fare,) Tj T*
(including confirmed PQ or waitlisted status. The single PNR booking service fee is also refunded) Tj T*
(once if all passengers on that PNR are affected by this operator cancellation. No ordinary) Tj T*
(cancellation charge or clerkage applies. A customer choosing not to board an operating train is) Tj T*
(not an operator cancellation. A late E1 claim is not eligible under E1.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(E2. MAJOR DEPARTURE DELAY AND NON-TRAVEL — OVERRIDES P-03 AND P-05) Tj T*
(If SPR officially reschedules departure from the passenger's origin by at least 180 minutes) Tj T*
(beyond its original scheduled departure, and the passenger elects not to travel and submits an) Tj T*
(E2 claim BEFORE the train's actual departure from that origin, the passenger receives 100% of) Tj T*
(base fare, including confirmed PQ fares; clerkage and ordinary cancellation fees do not apply.) Tj T*
(The booking service fee is not refunded. A passenger who boarded or submits only after actual) Tj T*
(departure cannot claim E2. A delay of one minute less than the threshold does not qualify.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(E3. CERTIFIED MEDICAL EMERGENCY — OVERRIDES ORDINARY TIME CUTOFFS) Tj T*
(If an affected passenger cannot travel because of an acute medical emergency certified by a) Tj T*
(licensed clinician with an examination documented before scheduled departure, an E3 claim filed) Tj T*
(within 24 hours AFTER scheduled departure can recover the passenger's base fare minus a flat) Tj T*
(medical deduction of INR 100 \(not below zero\), regardless of how close to departure the request) Tj T*
(is made. The claimant must not have boarded. Premium QuickBook passengers are excluded from E3.) Tj T*
(E3 does not reimburse the booking fee. This is a claim-based exception, not an automatic refund) Tj T*
(merely because a medical problem is alleged.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(E4. DOCUMENTED ACCIDENTAL DUPLICATE PURCHASE — OVERRIDES P-03 AND P-05) Tj T*
(If two separate PNRs are purchased for exactly the same passenger, train, travel date, origin,) Tj T*
(destination, and class, and the second purchase is identified as accidental within 15 minutes) Tj T*
(after that purchase and before scheduled departure, SPR refunds the full base fare on the SECOND) Tj T*
(PNR plus that second PNR's booking service fee; the first booking remains active. PQ status does) Tj T*
(not disqualify a genuine duplicate. The 15-minute limit is inclusive. A similar journey or a) Tj T*
(different class is not an exact duplicate. Merely cancelling the first PNR is not covered.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(E5. NOT IN FORCE — No separate evacuation exception exists.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(P-09. EXCLUSIONS AND INTERPRETIVE RULES) Tj T*
(Missed trains and personal changes of plan create no special refund beyond the ordinary) Tj T*
(provisions. A train running on time does not trigger E2; an advisory is not an official) Tj T*
(rescheduling. No waiver may be inferred merely because another passenger on the same PNR) Tj T*
(qualifies for an exception; eligible passengers are evaluated individually. In a mixed-status) Tj T*
(PNR, the special conditions of an exception apply only to affected passengers, except the) Tj T*
(single-fee treatment described in E1 and E4. All percentages are applied to the affected) Tj T*
(passenger's base fare, not to base fare plus booking fee. If a customer gives inconsistent dates) Tj T*
(or omits a necessary fact, SPR cannot unconditionally promise an exception refund.) Tj T*
ET
